    <item ident="g7a88c319536d74e15df64b54ad62ed03" title="Question">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>3485,3389,1608</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style="border: 6px solid #808080; padding: 5px;"&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Academic Honesty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students taking courses through BYU-Idaho are expected to follow BYU-Idaho's &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byui.edu/student-honor-office/ces-honor-code" target="_blank"&gt;Academic Honesty policy.&lt;/a&gt; This includes avoiding plagiarism, fabrication or falsification, cheating, academic misconduct, and unauthorized uploading or sharing. BYU-Idaho takes academic honesty seriously and violations of the Academic Honesty Policy may result in consequences up to and including suspension or expulsion from the university.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cody and Angie are both in the same course but in different sections. Cody needed to take Quiz 1, a timed open-note, open-book, but not an open-person test. Since he had been busy at his job and dating Angie, he did not finish reading the assigned chapters. He had planned on organizing his material before the test but needed to help his friend who was sick. Panicked, he called Angie who had already taken the quiz, and asked her what questions were on the quiz.&amp;nbsp; Was this academically honest?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="3485">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes, it is academically honest. Cody made an attempt to study but was too busy to finish the study guides.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="3389">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes. It is academically honest. It is important for students to help one another through difficult times.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="1608">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">No. It is not academically honest. Asking someone who has taken the test what was on it is academically dishonest.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">1608</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="g7e56b8558b4e5d9feaa33b7149586f3a" title="Question">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>4916,5947</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;This is the first course in the &lt;strong&gt;Web and Computer Programming Certificate&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;BYU-Pathway certificates list a technology level (see the &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byupathway.edu/technology-requirements" target="_blank"&gt;BYU-Pathway Technology Requirements&lt;/a&gt; for full details):&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile Device&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;: Smartphone (Android 9+ or iOS 14+)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Light Computing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: inherit; font-size: 1rem;"&gt;: Laptop that can run Microsoft Office (Word, Excel)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Heavy Computing&lt;/strong&gt;: Laptop that can run more demanding software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;All courses in the &lt;strong&gt;Web and Computer Programming Certificate&lt;/strong&gt; require &lt;strong&gt;Heavy Computing&lt;/strong&gt; (a laptop that can run more demanding software).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quick check&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Do you have access to a laptop that meets the &lt;strong&gt;Heavy Computing&lt;/strong&gt; requirement?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;(If you have further questions, please reach out to your instructor.)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="4916">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes, I have access to a laptop that can run more demanding software.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="5947">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">No, I don't have access to a laptop that can run more demanding software.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">5947</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="5947_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">4916</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="5947_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">If you answered that you don't have access to a laptop that can run more demanding software, please reach out to your instructor for help.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
