    <item ident="gbab16d17b7497ace466692f4ab1fa2aa" title="Question">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>true_false_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1730,6993</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;Turnitin is a program that lets you and your teachers know how much your work reflects other peoples work. After you have submitted your work there will be a color flag appear next to your submission in the grades tab. The different color flags will indicate the percentage of your submission that Turnitin has found to be copied. &lt;strong&gt;NOTE&lt;/strong&gt;: Assignments that use templates will have some copying and Turnitin will flag the assignment questions—do not worry about this. Make sure your answers to the questions have not been copied.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;If the color of your flag is red, you must rework your assignment and resubmit it until your flag is no longer red. An assignment that is turned in with the red flag will not be graded and will be given a 0.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 45.2639%; height: 271px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;" border="1"&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 29px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;Turnitin Score Icons&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 53px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 53px;"&gt;&lt;img id="6042618" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/assessment_questions/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20GrayFlag.PNG?canvas_download=1" alt="W01 Quiz: Syllabus GrayFlag.PNG" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 53px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gray&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(originality report has not been generated)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 44px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 44px;"&gt;&lt;img id="6042617" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/assessment_questions/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20BlueFlag.PNG?canvas_download=1" alt="W01 Quiz: Syllabus BlueFlag.PNG" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 44px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blue&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(no matching words)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 29px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;img id="6042621" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/assessment_questions/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20GreenFlag.PNG?canvas_download=1" alt="W01 Quiz: Syllabus GreenFlag.PNG" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Green&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(1-24% similarity index)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 29px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;img id="6042603" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/assessment_questions/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20YellowFlag.PNG?canvas_download=1" alt="W01 Quiz: Syllabus YellowFlag.PNG" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Yellow&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(25-49% similarity index)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 29px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;img id="6042619" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/assessment_questions/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20OrangeFlag.PNG?canvas_download=1" alt="W01 Quiz: Syllabus OrangeFlag.PNG" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orange&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(50-74% similarity index)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 29px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;img id="6042620" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/assessment_questions/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20RedFlag.PNG?canvas_download=1" alt="W01 Quiz: Syllabus RedFlag.PNG" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Red&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(75-100% similarity index)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 29px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 25.1206%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;img id="6042616" src="$IMS-CC-FILEBASE$/assessment_questions/W01%20Quiz:%20Syllabus%20Clock.PNG?canvas_download=1" alt="W01 Quiz: Syllabus Clock.PNG" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 74.8819%; height: 29px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clock&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(Turnitin report is still pending)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt;Turnitin can be used to provide immediate feedback so you will know what needs to be fixed before submitting your assignments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="1730">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">True</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6993">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">False</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">6993</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
    <item ident="g85f44bf53eadfb6f3e289903f1d418fa" title="Question">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>3485,3389,1608</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style="border: 6px solid #808080; padding: 5px;"&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Academic Honesty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students taking courses through BYU-Idaho are expected to follow BYU-Idaho's &lt;a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.byui.edu/student-honor-office/ces-honor-code" target="_blank"&gt;Academic Honesty policy.&lt;/a&gt; This includes avoiding plagiarism, fabrication or falsification, cheating, academic misconduct, and unauthorized uploading or sharing. BYU-Idaho takes academic honesty seriously and violations of the Academic Honesty Policy may result in consequences up to and including suspension or expulsion from the university.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cody and Angie are both in the same course but in different sections. Cody needed to take Quiz 1, a timed open-note, open-book, but not an open-person test. Since he had been busy at his job and dating Angie, he did not finish reading the assigned chapters. He had planned on organizing his material before the test but needed to help his friend who was sick. Panicked, he called Angie who had already taken the quiz, and asked her what questions were on the quiz.&amp;nbsp; Was this academically honest?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="3485">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Yes, it is academically honest. Cody made an attempt to study but was too busy to finish the study guides.</mattext>
              </material>
