          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>181,2401</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As part of the Church Educational System Honor Code, you are expected to complete your own work for each course.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you choose to participate in&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;any&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;actions which violate the Academic Honesty policy, the university has the right to&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;change your course grade to an F now or at any time in the future&lt;/strong&gt;. This means that even if your dishonesty is not discovered until after you complete your certificate or degree, the university still has the right to change your grade and&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;revoke your certificate or degree&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which of the following are violations of the Honor Code or Academic Honesty Policy? Note that this list is not exhaustive (see Jacob 6:12).&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mark all that apply.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Multiple">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="181">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain"></mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="2401">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain"></mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <and>
              <varequal respident="response1">181</varequal>
              <not>
                <varequal respident="response1">2401</varequal>
              </not>
            </and>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
    </item>
